      "text": "Djenné’s mud architecture is remarkable because maintenance is built into the life of the building itself. 🇲🇱🏛 Instead of expecting walls to survive untouched for centuries, communities periodically repair them together after weathering and rain. It turns architecture into an ongoing social tradition rather than a finished object, which is a very different idea of preservation.",
